  {
    "id": "bdd7ed7605b867f58c55",
    "source": "Opportunity attacks are automatic on BOTH sides: when a player walks out of an enemy's reach the server rolls the enemy's swing, and when you move an enemy out of a character's reach with move_token the server rolls that character's swing and applies it. Both post as table notes and come back on the move_token result. Never narrate a free retreat in either direction, never roll one yourself, and never call pc_attack or use_reaction for one on a battle map; off the map, a character's opportunity attack is use_reaction with targetEnemyId. When the last enemy falls to an opportunity attack the fight does not end by itself: narrate it and call end_encounter with outcome victory. Hiding is real too: take_action hide (in a fight only; out of one it is a Stealth request_roll against check_notice) compares their Stealth against the enemies' actual passive Perception, and a successful hide gives their next attack advantage and is spent by making it.",
    "sourceHash": "bdd7ed7605b867f58c55d5e93b5813abc39cc6cb157044274fb1d88babf48e9d",
    "kinds": [
      "display-property"
    ],
    "sites": [
